# Organize without redesign

When cleaning up or restructuring code (Ask Ulo, onboarding, dashboards, edge functions):

## The main rule

**First, move the existing code into better-organized files.**

Do **not** redesign the product experience in the same pull request.

## Goal

| Keep identical | Change freely |
|---|---|
| Screens, copy, buttons | File layout, module names |
| Save / submit behavior | Stage boundaries, re-exports |
| Navigation | Thin orchestrators that call the same helpers |
| Completion / activation process | Tests and docs that describe the move |
| Answers, refuse/clarify, tool packets (Ask Ulo) | Where lookups live (as long as packets match) |

Better-organized code underneath — same thing for the user.

## How to work

1. **Move first** — extract helpers, split stages, add shims/re-exports so callers stay stable.
2. **Preserve contracts** — same function inputs/outputs, same DB writes, same SMS/email copy, same packet shapes.
3. **One concern per PR** — organization only. No “while we’re here” UX or policy changes.
4. **Park product decisions** — anything that needs “should we show X instead?” goes in a later PR.

## Tests before merge

- Same user-visible path still works (same screens / same Ask Ulo answers for the same questions).
- Prefer behavioral tests or gold-set checks over “it compiles.”

## What not to do

- Redesign onboarding steps, Ask Ulo answer format, or verification UX in a cleanup PR
- Change refuse/clarify/prefer policy while renaming files
- Delete a dual path until the new path returns the **same** packets
- Mix “wrap as domain tool” with “change when that tool runs” in one PR
